fluxecho.module.resonance_gate=Resonance Gate
tile.fluxecho.module_core.resonance_gate.name=Resonance Gate Core
fluxecho.resonance_gate.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's gate§r\nTwo wing towers either side of the gate road joined by a bridge, a crystal spire floating and slowly turning over it\nIts resonators and tuning racks keep the team's samples; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.resonance_gate.structure=§bThe Resonance Gate: a gatehouse 31×17 and 18 high§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on the gate (site 0) once the Resonance Gate is researched (phase II): the nexus projects it; supply the core and materials and press Start\n· Two wing towers (9×17 each) stand either side of the gate road, the passage between them 13 wide and 7 high left open: the gate road, its widenings and the four pylons stay as they are, and only the ground the road leaves bare is floored\n· Each wing has a ground hall (a front door and a door onto the passage) and a spiral stair up to its upper hall 8 blocks up; both upper halls open into the resonance chamber on the bridge, whose core column gives way to a rendered crystal spire once it forms\n· 10 units, 24 samples: 6 resonator columns (2 samples each) in the resonance chamber and 4 tuning racks (3 samples each) on the halls' outer walls; a unit is used as a whole: right-click any part of it holding a sample to set it, empty-handed to open the gate; sneak-click a socket empty-handed to take its sample back\n· The core on the Console Stand of the kiosk in the road under the bridge, two blocks above the foundation, in reach from the road\n· Made of Module Foundation and frame parts, Campus Deck and Wall Panels, Steel Glaze, posts, plinths, crowns, treads, holo pedestals, Sample Sockets and Cladding Anchors (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
